---

<section id="about" class="relative py-28 md:py-36">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 md:px-8">
    <div class="grid items-center gap-14 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-20">
      <!-- [PLACEHOLDER: Sergio studio/artist photo — neon interior] -->
      <div class="gallery-piece aspect-[4/5] max-w-xl" data-reveal>
        <img
          src="/images/about-sergio.svg"
          alt="Sergio Furlan at work in his neon-lit Dublin studio — placeholder for artist portrait"
          class="h-full w-full object-cover"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </div>

      <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="0.15">
        <p class="section-kicker mb-4">About</p>
        <h2 class="section-title text-4xl md:text-5xl">Art. Attitude.<br />Identity.</h2>

        <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[0.98rem] leading-relaxed text-bone-dim">
          <p>
            [PLACEHOLDER: Sergio's real bio — background, years tattooing,
            journey to Dublin.] Sergio Furlan builds tattoos the way a painter
            builds a canvas — layered, deliberate, made to last. His name was
            made on black &amp; grey depth and colour realism that stays
            saturated long after it heals.
          </p>
          <p>
            It's the cover up work that says the most about how he operates.
            Taking a tattoo someone has regretted for years and turning it into
            the piece they lead with takes more than technique — it takes
            trust, honest consultation, and a designer's eye for what the skin
            will actually allow. That trust is the core of the studio.
          </p>
          <p>
            Every piece starts with a conversation: your idea, your placement,
            your story — then his drawing. No flash-rack shortcuts.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-3 gap-6 border-t border-white/10 pt-8">
          {
            [
              { stat: '10+', label: 'Years tattooing' },
              { stat: '260+', label: 'Pieces published' },
              { stat: 'Dublin', label: 'Private studio' },
            ].map(({ stat, label }) => (
              <div>
                <p class="font-display text-3xl font-medium text-blood">{stat}</p>
                <p class="mt-1 text-[0.72rem] tracking-[0.18em] uppercase text-bone-dim">{label}</p>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
